Z||000000||Wolfhound||03-04-2001||05:32 AM||||Saturday of last week I picked up a 86 SE V6 Automatic. This car has an odd history of bad luck. It never seemed to get off the ground from the day of purchase. I removed it from a blackberry patch where it tree had fallen on it when hurricane Opal came up through Alabama in October of 95. Here are some photos of the car when I first got it home. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc1.JPG"> <BR>The interior was filled with leaves  and broken glass. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc2.JPG">  <BR>The under hood area speaks for it,s self<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc3.JPG"> <BR>The engine compartment was filled with blackberry briers and vines, at this  point I had removed most of them.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc4.JPG">  <BR>When I got it home I began checking it out closer, and saw this!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc5.JPG">  <BR>and this<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/resc6.JPG"> <BR>This week it has got good cleaning so I could see what i was working on. a windshield, gas tank and fuel pump, headlight motor unit, front sub bumper and plastic energy absorber after a little BFH work on the area in front the passenger headlight, hood and headlight covers, right front brake caliper,and hey it runs fine. Still lots to do! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroSEt||03-04-2001||01:54 PM||||great save...  I just save a 86 SE 2m6 from a pasture after it sat there for almost 5 year's...  it had a bad motor, but I just swapped it outta my 87GT part's car. I got it for $200.00!!!! <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||03-04-2001||02:04 PM||||Damn whats all that crap in the engine comparment?  Almost looks like a bunch of burnt shoe strings or something.  Good luck rescuing that car!  Looks like a worthy project...||||reg||1
